<style>
  .delivery-date-options-custom {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 10px;
    margin-top: 6px;
  }

  .delivery-date-label-custom {
    font-size: 13px;
    margin-bottom: 6px;
    display: block;
  }

  /* The field was skipped. The words are the same words — they were always
     the instruction — so this is emphasis, not information, and nothing is
     inserted or repeated. */
  .delivery-date-label-custom.delivery-date-missing {
    color: #b3261e;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .delivery-date-button-custom {
    padding: 1rem 2rem;
    border: 1px solid #d3d3d3;
    border-radius: 25px;
    background: #fff;
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: 0.12s ease;
  }

  .delivery-date-button-custom:hover {
    border-color: #000;
  }

  .delivery-date-button-custom.active-custom {
    background: #000;
    color: #fff;
    border-color: #000;
  }

  .delivery-date-wrapper-custom {
    margin-top: 12px;
  }
</style>

{% assign current_domain = request.host | downcase | remove: 'www.' %}

{% comment %}
  Rules target a market code (e.g. "de"), with "main" for the primary market
  on the bare domain. Markets moved from subdomains to subfolders, so the code
  comes from the URL prefix ("/de-de" -> "de"); request.host is now identical
  for every market and can no longer distinguish them. A legacy subdomain
  hostname still resolves, so old rules keep working if such a domain is hit.
{% endcomment %}
{% assign current_subdomain = 'main' %}
{% if routes.root_url != '/' %}
  {% assign current_subdomain = routes.root_url | remove_first: '/' | split: '-' | last | downcase %}
{% else %}
  {% assign host_parts = current_domain | split: '.' %}
  {% if host_parts.size > 2 %}
    {% assign current_subdomain = host_parts | first %}
  {% endif %}
{% endif %}

{% comment %}
  OUR name for the market, beside Shopify's own token above.

  The path prefix speaks ISO country codes — /en-gb, /en-de — while the admin,
  the warehouses and the people all say UK and EU, so a stored market list
  compared against the raw token misses Britain entirely ('gb' against 'uk')
  and misses every country inside a grouped market. The `warehouse`
  metaobjects already carry the mapping — each lists the domains it serves —
  so this reads it there: the handle's head IS our code ('uk-3-pl' -> 'uk').

  Canada has no XX 3PL location and its warehouse is named for the 3PL
  instead, so its head is not 'ca' — which is why BOTH this and the raw token
  are matched below rather than one replacing the other.

  This is a second copy of the derivation in `sections/popup-signup.liquid`,
  which did it first. A shared snippet cannot assign back to its caller —
  render is scope-isolated and include is deprecated — so the two are kept in
  step by hand: a change to either belongs in both.
{% endcomment %}
{% assign dd_wh = '' %}
{% assign dd_wh_default = '' %}
{% for wh in settings.warehouses %}
  {% assign dd_h = wh.system.handle | downcase %}
  {% if wh.is_default.value and dd_wh_default == '' %}
    {% assign dd_wh_default = dd_h %}
  {% endif %}
  {% if wh.domains.value %}
    {% for dd_d in wh.domains.value %}
      {% assign dd_dd = dd_d | strip | downcase %}
      {% if dd_dd == current_subdomain %}
        {% assign dd_wh = dd_h %}
      {% endif %}
    {% endfor %}
  {% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% if dd_wh == '' %}{% assign dd_wh = dd_wh_default %}{% endif %}

{% comment %}
  The root domain is the primary market — what the admin calls rest of world.
  No warehouse head spells it, so it is named here.
{% endcomment %}
{% if current_subdomain == 'main' %}
  {% assign market_code = 'primary' %}
{% elsif dd_wh != '' %}
  {% assign market_code = dd_wh | split: '-' | first %}
{% else %}
  {% assign market_code = current_subdomain %}
{% endif %}

{% comment %}
  This product's SKUs, which is how an option says who it applies to.

  Matched on the SKU rather than the handle or the title: a title can be
  edited and the handle changes with it, while a SKU is what the 3PL, the
  rate engine and the BI pipeline all key off. The admin publishes WHOLE SKUs
  as the store spells them — `SC26`, `VC26W`, `HL06` — read out of the store's
  own catalogue, so this file needs to know nothing about how they are put
  together and no prefix rule can go subtly wrong.

  Every variant's SKU is collected, not just the selected one: a product page
  offers the same dispatch dates whichever colourway is showing, and reading
  only the current variant would change the buttons as somebody clicked
  between them.
{% endcomment %}
{% assign product_skus = '' %}
{% for dd_v in product.variants %}
  {% assign dd_s = dd_v.sku | strip | upcase %}
  {% if dd_s != blank %}
    {% assign product_skus = product_skus | append: dd_s | append: '||' %}
  {% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% assign product_skus = product_skus | split: '||' %}

{% comment %}
  Per-product exclusions (custom.delivery_domain_rule metafield):
  entries of { domain, exclude_date } hide the named dates on that domain
  for this product only. Applies to both data sources below.
{% endcomment %}
{% assign rule_list = product.metafields.custom.delivery_domain_rule.value %}
{% assign excluded_raw = '' %}

{% if rule_list %}
  {% for entry in rule_list %}
    {% assign entry_domain = entry.domain | downcase | remove: 'www.' | strip %}

    {% if entry_domain == current_domain or entry_domain == current_subdomain %}
      {% assign exclude_string = entry.exclude_date | strip %}

      {% if exclude_string != '' %}
        {% assign exclude_array = exclude_string | split: ',' %}
        {% for ex in exclude_array %}
          {% assign ex_clean = ex | strip %}
          {% assign excluded_raw = excluded_raw | append: ex_clean | append: '||' %}
        {% endfor %}
      {% endif %}
    {% endif %}
  {% endfor %}
{% endif %}

{% assign excluded = excluded_raw | split: '||' | uniq %}

{% assign final_list = '' %}
{% assign label_list = '' %}

{% comment %}
  Source 1: the admin's own document, published as ranked
  `delivery_date_option` entries.

  Behind `settings.dispatch_from_admin`, which ships OFF: with it off this
  file behaves exactly as it did, so merging the change puts nothing on the
  shop. Turning it on is the rollout, and turning it off again is the
  rollback — seconds, no deploy.

  **Ranks are walked explicitly.** Iteration order is not guaranteed, and
  `sort: 'rank'` does not fix it: a metaobject field is an object, so sorting
  on 'rank' sorts the wrapper rather than the number inside it, silently
  returns the source order, and raises nothing. At a ceiling of a dozen
  options the nested loop is trivial and relies on no undocumented behaviour.
{% endcomment %}
{% comment %}
  The switch is not enough on its own: the store ALREADY carries hand-made
  `delivery_date_option` entries, the ones the picked list below renders. They
  have no rank — the field did not exist when they were made — so the walk
  below matches none of them, and a guard that only asked whether any entries
  exist would hand this file a source it draws nothing from. The picker would
  empty on the first flip of the switch.

  So the question is whether anything RANKED is published, which is the same
  as asking whether the admin has published at all.
{% endcomment %}
{% assign dd_ranked = 0 %}
{% for dd_e in metaobjects.delivery_date_option.values %}
  {% if dd_e.rank.value != blank %}
    {% assign dd_ranked = dd_ranked | plus: 1 %}
  {% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% assign dd_from_admin = false %}
{% if settings.dispatch_from_admin and dd_ranked > 0 %}
  {% assign dd_from_admin = true %}
{% endif %}

{% if dd_from_admin %}
  {% assign month_keys = 'jan,feb,mar,apr,may,jun,jul,aug,sep,oct,nov,dec' | split: ',' %}
  {% assign months_en = 'Jan,Feb,Mar,Apr,May,Jun,Jul,Aug,Sep,Oct,Nov,Dec' | split: ',' %}
  {% assign today_num = 'now' | date: '%Y%m%d' | plus: 0 %}
  {% assign today_mmdd = 'now' | date: '%m%d' | plus: 0 %}

  {% for rank_i in (1..24) %}
    {% for entry in metaobjects.delivery_date_option.values %}
      {% if entry.rank.value != rank_i %}{% continue %}{% endif %}

      {% comment %} The window. Both ends are the store's own clock. {% endcomment %}
      {% if entry.show_on.value != blank %}
        {% assign show_num = entry.show_on.value | date: '%Y%m%d' | plus: 0 %}
        {% if today_num < show_num %}{% continue %}{% endif %}
      {% endif %}
      {% if entry.hide_after.value != blank %}
        {% assign hide_num = entry.hide_after.value | date: '%Y%m%d' | plus: 0 %}
        {% if today_num > hide_num %}{% continue %}{% endif %}
      {% endif %}

      {% comment %}
        Markets, as an INCLUDE list. Both our code and Shopify's token are
        matched, because Canada's warehouse head is not 'ca' — see above. An
        entry with no list at all is offered everywhere rather than nowhere:
        a field that has not been written yet must not empty the shop.
      {% endcomment %}
      {% if entry.markets.value and entry.markets.value.size > 0 %}
        {% assign dd_ok = false %}
        {% for dd_m in entry.markets.value %}
          {% assign dd_mm = dd_m | strip | downcase %}
          {% if dd_mm == market_code or dd_mm == current_subdomain %}
            {% assign dd_ok = true %}
            {% break %}
          {% endif %}
        {% endfor %}
        {% unless dd_ok %}{% continue %}{% endunless %}
      {% endif %}

      {% comment %}
        Products, by whole SKU. Equality, not a prefix: the admin publishes
        what the store itself spells, so there is nothing to be clever about
        and no `SC` quietly matching `SCARF01`.

        An entry naming no SKUs applies to everything, as with the markets. An
        entry that DOES name them applies only where one matches — including
        when the product has no SKU at all, which cannot match anything. That
        is the conservative reading and it is uniform: a product nobody
        configured is offered no dispatch date rather than silently inheriting
        every one of them. It loses only the picker, not the sale — with no
        buttons the field stops being required.

        One thing this cannot do: the buttons are one control for the whole
        product page, drawn outside the variant chooser, so naming a single
        colourway shows the option whenever ANY variant of that product is on
        screen. Per-colourway control would be a different change.
      {% endcomment %}
      {% if entry.skus.value and entry.skus.value.size > 0 %}
        {% assign dd_pok = false %}
        {% for dd_p in entry.skus.value %}
          {% assign dd_pp = dd_p | strip | upcase %}
          {% if dd_pp == blank %}{% continue %}{% endif %}
          {% for dd_s in product_skus %}
            {% if dd_s == dd_pp %}
              {% assign dd_pok = true %}
              {% break %}
            {% endif %}
          {% endfor %}
          {% if dd_pok %}{% break %}{% endif %}
        {% endfor %}
        {% unless dd_pok %}{% continue %}{% endunless %}
      {% endif %}

      {% comment %}
        The value the ORDER carries, and the label a customer reads. The value
        is always English — per-product exclusion rules match it verbatim and
        every past order carries it — while the label is localised, or
        overridden by the entry's own.
      {% endcomment %}
      {% assign special = entry.special.value | strip %}
      {% assign date_string = '' %}
      {% assign generated_label = '' %}

      {% if special != blank %}
        {% assign date_string = special %}
        {% assign special_down = special | downcase %}
        {% if special_down == 'asap' %}
          {% assign generated_label = 'delivery.date_options.asap' | t %}
        {% elsif special_down == 'by xmas' or special_down == 'by christmas' %}
          {% if today_mmdd > 1225 %}{% continue %}{% endif %}
          {% assign generated_label = 'delivery.date_options.by_xmas' | t %}
        {% else %}
          {% assign generated_label = special %}
        {% endif %}
      {% elsif entry.date.value %}
        {% assign date_num = entry.date.value | date: '%Y%m%d' | plus: 0 %}
        {% if today_num > date_num %}{% continue %}{% endif %}
        {% assign day_num = entry.date.value | date: '%d' | plus: 0 %}
        {% assign month_index = entry.date.value | date: '%m' | plus: 0 | minus: 1 %}
        {% assign date_string = day_num | append: ' ' | append: months_en[month_index] %}
        {% assign month_key = 'delivery.months.' | append: month_keys[month_index] %}
        {% assign month_translated = month_key | t %}
        {% assign generated_label = 'delivery.date_label' | t: day: day_num, month: month_translated %}
      {% else %}
        {% continue %}
      {% endif %}

      {% comment %} The per-product metafield still has the last word. {% endcomment %}
      {% if excluded contains date_string %}{% continue %}{% endif %}

      {% assign custom_label = entry.label.value | default: '' | strip %}
      {% if custom_label != blank %}
        {% assign generated_label = custom_label %}
      {% endif %}

      {% assign final_list = final_list | append: date_string | append: '||' %}
      {% assign label_list = label_list | append: generated_label | append: '||' %}
    {% endfor %}
  {% endfor %}

{% elsif settings.delivery_date_entries.count > 0 %}
  {% comment %}
    Primary source: "Delivery date option" metaobjects picked in theme settings.
    Field keys:
      date    - real date field (picker); auto-hides once the date has passed
      special - non-date options: "ASAP" or "By Xmas" (used when date is empty)
      label   - optional display override, translatable via T Lab
      hide_on - list of subdomain codes / hostnames, "main" = bare domain
      expires - optional date; entry hidden after this day (mainly for specials)
    The value stored on the order (data-date) is always English: "10 Dec",
    "ASAP" or "By Xmas". The displayed label is localized via the theme
    locale keys delivery.date_label / delivery.months.* / delivery.date_options.*.
  {% endcomment %}
  {% assign month_keys = 'jan,feb,mar,apr,may,jun,jul,aug,sep,oct,nov,dec' | split: ',' %}
  {% assign months_en = 'Jan,Feb,Mar,Apr,May,Jun,Jul,Aug,Sep,Oct,Nov,Dec' | split: ',' %}
  {% assign today_num = 'now' | date: '%Y%m%d' | plus: 0 %}
  {% assign today_mmdd = 'now' | date: '%m%d' | plus: 0 %}

  {% for entry in settings.delivery_date_entries %}
    {% assign special = entry.special.value | strip %}
    {% assign date_string = '' %}
    {% assign generated_label = '' %}

    {% if special != blank %}
      {% assign date_string = special %}
      {% assign special_down = special | downcase %}
      {% if special_down == 'asap' %}
        {% assign generated_label = 'delivery.date_options.asap' | t %}
      {% elsif special_down == 'by xmas' or special_down == 'by christmas' %}
        {% if today_mmdd > 1225 %}{% continue %}{% endif %}
        {% assign generated_label = 'delivery.date_options.by_xmas' | t %}
      {% else %}
        {% assign generated_label = special %}
      {% endif %}
    {% elsif entry.date.value %}
      {% assign date_num = entry.date.value | date: '%Y%m%d' | plus: 0 %}
      {% if today_num > date_num %}{% continue %}{% endif %}

      {% assign day_num = entry.date.value | date: '%d' | plus: 0 %}
      {% assign month_index = entry.date.value | date: '%m' | plus: 0 | minus: 1 %}
      {% assign date_string = day_num | append: ' ' | append: months_en[month_index] %}

      {% assign month_key = 'delivery.months.' | append: month_keys[month_index] %}
      {% assign month_translated = month_key | t %}
      {% assign generated_label = 'delivery.date_label' | t: day: day_num, month: month_translated %}
    {% else %}
      {% continue %}
    {% endif %}

    {% if excluded contains date_string %}{% continue %}{% endif %}

    {% assign hidden_here = false %}
    {% if entry.hide_on.value %}
      {% for h in entry.hide_on.value %}
        {% assign h_clean = h | downcase | remove: 'www.' | strip %}
        {% if h_clean == current_domain or h_clean == current_subdomain %}
          {% assign hidden_here = true %}
        {% endif %}
      {% endfor %}
    {% endif %}
    {% if hidden_here %}{% continue %}{% endif %}

    {% if entry.expires.value %}
      {% assign expires_num = entry.expires.value | date: '%Y%m%d' | plus: 0 %}
      {% if today_num > expires_num %}{% continue %}{% endif %}
    {% endif %}

    {% assign custom_label = entry.label.value | default: '' | strip %}
    {% if custom_label != blank %}
      {% assign generated_label = custom_label %}
    {% endif %}

    {% assign final_list = final_list | append: date_string | append: '||' %}
    {% assign label_list = label_list | append: generated_label | append: '||' %}
  {% endfor %}
{% else %}
  {% comment %} Legacy fallback: comma-separated list from theme settings. {% endcomment %}
  {% assign cleaned_text = settings.delivery_dates | strip_html | strip %}
  {% assign global_dates = cleaned_text | split: ',' %}

  {% for d in global_dates %}
    {% assign dd = d | strip %}
    {% if dd != '' %}
      {% unless excluded contains dd %}
        {% assign final_list = final_list | append: dd | append: '||' %}
      {% endunless %}
    {% endif %}
  {% endfor %}
{% endif %}

{% assign final_dates = final_list | split: '||' %}
{% assign final_labels = label_list | split: '||' %}

<div class="delivery-date-wrapper-custom">
  {%- comment -%}
    One string, not two. This label used to read "Choose Delivery Date" while
    a second key, `delivery.required_message`, said "Choose a delivery date"
    in red beneath it the moment somebody skipped the field — the same
    sentence twice, stacked. The instruction is permanent now and the error
    turns THIS red, so nothing is inserted and nothing is repeated.

    Colour is not carrying the meaning: the words say what to do whether or
    not anybody has ignored them. The red is emphasis on an instruction that
    was already there.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <label class="delivery-date-label-custom" id="delivery-date-label-custom">{{ 'delivery.choose_date' | t }}</label>

  <div class="delivery-date-options-custom">
    {% for d in final_dates %}
      {% if d != '' %}
        {% assign raw_date = d | strip %}
        {% assign normalized_date = raw_date | downcase %}
        {% assign button_label = raw_date %}
        {% assign is_asap = false %}
        {% assign custom_label = final_labels[forloop.index0] %}

        {% if normalized_date == 'asap' %}
          {% assign is_asap = true %}
        {% endif %}

        {% if custom_label != blank %}
          {% assign button_label = custom_label %}
        {% elsif normalized_date == 'asap' %}
          {% assign button_label = 'delivery.date_options.asap' | t %}
        {% elsif normalized_date == 'by xmas' or normalized_date == 'by christmas' %}
          {% assign button_label = 'delivery.date_options.by_xmas' | t %}
        {% else %}
          {% assign date_parts = raw_date | split: ' ' %}
          {% if date_parts.size == 2 %}
            {% assign day_part = date_parts[0] | remove: ',' %}
            {% assign month_part = date_parts[1] | remove: ',' | downcase %}
            {% assign month_translation = '' %}

            {% case month_part %}
              {% when 'jan' %}
                {% assign month_translation = 'delivery.months.jan' | t %}
              {% when 'january' %}
                {% assign month_translation = 'delivery.months.jan' | t %}
              {% when 'feb' %}
                {% assign month_translation = 'delivery.months.feb' | t %}
              {% when 'february' %}
                {% assign month_translation = 'delivery.months.feb' | t %}
              {% when 'mar' %}
                {% assign month_translation = 'delivery.months.mar' | t %}
              {% when 'march' %}
                {% assign month_translation = 'delivery.months.mar' | t %}
              {% when 'apr' %}
                {% assign month_translation = 'delivery.months.apr' | t %}
              {% when 'april' %}
                {% assign month_translation = 'delivery.months.apr' | t %}
              {% when 'may' %}
                {% assign month_translation = 'delivery.months.may' | t %}
              {% when 'jun' %}
                {% assign month_translation = 'delivery.months.jun' | t %}
              {% when 'june' %}
                {% assign month_translation = 'delivery.months.jun' | t %}
              {% when 'jul' %}
                {% assign month_translation = 'delivery.months.jul' | t %}
              {% when 'july' %}
                {% assign month_translation = 'delivery.months.jul' | t %}
              {% when 'aug' %}
                {% assign month_translation = 'delivery.months.aug' | t %}
              {% when 'august' %}
                {% assign month_translation = 'delivery.months.aug' | t %}
              {% when 'Sep' %}
                {% assign month_translation = 'delivery.months.sep' | t %}
              {% when 'sept' %}
                {% assign month_translation = 'delivery.months.sep' | t %}
              {% when 'september' %}
                {% assign month_translation = 'delivery.months.sep' | t %}
              {% when 'oct' %}
                {% assign month_translation = 'delivery.months.oct' | t %}
              {% when 'october' %}
                {% assign month_translation = 'delivery.months.oct' | t %}
              {% when 'nov' %}
                {% assign month_translation = 'delivery.months.nov' | t %}
              {% when 'november' %}
                {% assign month_translation = 'delivery.months.nov' | t %}
              {% when 'dec' %}
                {% assign month_translation = 'delivery.months.dec' | t %}
              {% when 'december' %}
                {% assign month_translation = 'delivery.months.dec' | t %}
            {% endcase %}

            {% if month_translation != '' %}
              {% assign button_label = day_part | append: ' ' | append: month_translation %}
            {% endif %}
          {% endif %}
        {% endif %}

        <button
          type="button"
          class="delivery-date-button-custom"
          data-date="{{ raw_date }}"
          {% if is_asap %}
            data-is-asap="true"
          {% endif %}
        >
          {{ button_label }}
        </button>
      {% endif %}
    {% endfor %}
  </div>

  <input
    type="hidden"
    name="properties[Delivery Date]"
    id="delivery-date-input-custom"
    required
  >
</div>
